"The shrine is the Wayfarer's: a small Divine of roads and those who travel them."
"Brannagh Tull in Merrowgate is the last who knows the Wayfarer's name, from her grandmother."
"The currents here have thinned since Nala woke; the crossing gave most of itself to make her."
"A worn inscription under the shrine's moss reads, in the old tongue: Keep the ones who wander."
